# AI Feature Rules

AI accelerates the product but is never the source of truth.

## AI may

- Explain findings and requirements in developer language
- Locate relevant code and likely root causes
- Propose remediations and generate candidate code/config changes
- Generate tests and summarize evidence

## AI must never

- Set or change a requirement/finding status directly
- Mark a remediation as `verified`
- Produce evidence records on its own authority
- Auto-apply changes without an explicit human approval step

## Implementation requirements

- All AI output is parsed into typed, validated structures (e.g. zod schemas) before use; reject or flag unparseable output.
- Persisted AI-generated content carries provenance metadata: model, timestamp, prompt/feature identifier, and an `ai_generated: true` flag surfaced in the UI.
- AI-suggested remediations enter the workflow at `suggested`, never further.
- Include a confidence field on AI explanations/suggestions and display it to users.
- Deterministic checks (static analysis, tests) are the only automated path to `passed`/`failed`/`verified`.
